;;; Written for this review: `happy` is written only as an activator's
;;; argument, passed to the parameter ?R that heads `tag`'s conclusion. A goal over
;;; `happy` loads (Q-M1f.119's "passes where a relation's name is held"), and has
;;; a row.

(person Ann)
(rule tag (?R) :match (person ?x) :assert (?R ?x) :why "every person is {?R}")
(tag happy)
(query :goal (happy ?x))
